The libc crate's Radix module (ADR 0070): the types, structures,
constants and functions of the C library, mlibc, on x86-64, as its
headers declare them. They are Linux's numbers and layouts, but for
mlibc's own pthread types, which are opaque or hold a pointer. The
constants were generated from the headers, and the rust-std port checks
every structure's size and layout and every constant against the headers
when it is built.

